course: dictionary
lesson: 11108
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word whip can be a thing you hold or a way of moving. «She whipped out her phone.» Nobody hit a phone with a whip here. The writer means she pulled it out very fast.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In «Whip the cream until it is thick», the cooking words tell you whip means beat fast. In «The rider cracked her whip», the word rider and the crack tell you it is the long thin rope. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Some meanings are only used in certain places or groups. In UK politics, a whip is a person who makes sure members of their party vote together. Some phrases have their own meaning too: «whip up» means make something quickly, and «whip round» means collect money from a group.
fact: A whip is a long thin rope or strip of leather with a handle.
fact: To whip means to hit with a whip, or to move something very fast.
fact: To whip cream or eggs means to beat them fast until they are thick and fluffy.
fact: «Whip up» means make something quickly.
fact: «Whip round» (UK) means collect money from a group of people.
fact: In politics, a whip is a person in parliament who makes sure the members of their party vote the party way.
exercise: «She whipped out her phone.» What does whipped mean here? | Hit it with a whip | Beat it until fluffy | *Moved very fast, pulling it out quickly | Dropped it on the floor
exercise: In cooking, to whip cream means what? | Pour it slowly into a jug | Freeze it solid in a tray | Hit it with a rope | *Beat it fast until thick and fluffy
exercise: «A whip is the person in a party who tries to make sure its members vote the party way.» What is a whip in this sentence? | A bird that flies very fast | A long thin rope used on horses | *A person who makes sure party members vote together | A rebel who votes against their party
test: «Let's whip up a snack before the film starts.» What does whip up mean? | Eat it very slowly | Throw it in the bin | *Make something quickly | Hit the snack with a whip
test: Dancers spot one point and whip their head round to find it again. What does whip their head round mean? | Hit it with a whip | Nod it up and down gently | *Turn it quickly and suddenly | Turn it slowly and carefully
exam: The class will whip round to collect money for a birthday card. What does whip round mean? | *Collect money from a group | Clean the classroom floor | Spin a rope in a circle | Fly away very quickly
